---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="Terms and Conditions of HabitTrack — free, client-side, local-first habit tracking application."
>
  <article class="max-w-none">
    <div class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-purple-900/50 pb-8">
      <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-600 dark:text-purple-400 bg-indigo-50 dark:bg-purple-950/60 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-indigo-100 dark:border-purple-800/60 mb-3">
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-50">
        Terms & Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-200/80 leading-relaxed">
        Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-purple-100/90 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using the HabitTrack web application ("the Application"), you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If you do not agree to these terms, please do not use the Application.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">2. Use License</h2>
        <p>
          HabitTrack is provided to you free of charge for personal, non-commercial, and self-improvement purposes. You may access the Application via standard web browsers and install it as a Progressive Web App (PWA).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">3. Local Data Responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          Because HabitTrack is an offline-first, client-only application, all habit information and records are stored exclusively within your browser's IndexedDB storage.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-sm sm:text-base">
          <li>We do not maintain server-side backups of your habits or logs.</li>
          <li>Clearing browser storage, uninstalling browser instances, or operating in private browsing modes may permanently erase your stored records.</li>
          <li>You are solely responsible for safeguarding and managing your local device environment.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">4. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The Application is provided on an <strong>"AS IS"</strong> and <strong>"AS AVAILABLE"</strong> basis without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied. We do not warrant that the Application will be error-free, uninterrupted, or compatible with every browser configuration or operating system.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          In no event shall the creators, maintainers, or contributors of HabitTrack be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including without limitation, loss of data, personal time, or productivity resulting from your use of or inability to use the Application.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">6. Modifications to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to revise or modify these Terms & Conditions at any time. Any changes become effective immediately upon posting to this URL.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
